@startuml building-blocks-bgz-referral
title "BGZ referral: building blocks stacked in a concrete exchange"
autonumber
skinparam roundCorner 7
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderThickness .5

participant "Placer\n(URA 11111111)" as P order 10
participant "Fulfiller\n(URA 22222222)" as F order 20

== Pre-coordination: two long-lived Subscriptions per partner pair ==
note over P, F #FFF2CC
  Workflow channel (Notification + NP):
  Topic: Coordination Task changes.
  Filter: Task?owner.identifier=URA|22222222.

  Data channel (Notification + NP):
  Topic: data offer changes.
  Filter: List?intended-recipient.identifier=URA|22222222.

  Both Subscriptions are hosted at the Placer and long-lived
  with the partnership.
end note

== CW: Order placed at Placer ==
P -> P : Create ServiceRequest (the Order, BgZ dataset)\n+ Coordination Task\n(Task.status = requested,\nTask.businessStatus = requested,\nTask.for.identifier = BSN 999911120)

== Notification + NP on the Coordination Task ==
P -> F ++: POST notification Bundle\nfocus = Coordination Task\nadditional-context = ServiceRequest (optional)
F --> P --: 200 OK
F -> P ++: GET Coordination Task\n(_include Task.focus = ServiceRequest)
P --> F --: 200 OK\nTask + ServiceRequest
note right of F #D5E8D4
  NP pull on the workflow anchor.
  BSN read from Task.for.identifier.
  PlanDefinition canonical from
  ServiceRequest.instantiatesCanonical
  is informative only: it declares
  which dataset to expect.
  The Receiver does not run its queries.
end note

== CW: Fulfiller accepts (write-back to Placer) ==
F -> P ++: PUT Coordination Task\n(Task.status = accepted,\nTask.businessStatus = accepted)
P --> F --: 200 OK

== Placer pre-resolves the dataset ==
P -> P : Evaluate the BgZ PlanDefinition\n(and any per-case additions)\nagainst local data.\nAssemble a flat List of concrete references\n(Patient, Conditions, MedicationStatements,\nObservations, ...).\nSet List.intended-recipient = Fulfiller URA\nso the existing data Subscription matches.

== Notification + NP on the dataset ==
P -> F ++: POST notification Bundle\nfocus = List (BgZ snapshot)
F --> P --: 200 OK
F -> P ++: GET List with _include entries
P --> F --: 200 OK\nList + BgZ resources
note right of F #D5E8D4
  NP pull on the data anchor.
  The Receiver follows List.entry refs;
  no query execution at the Receiver.
  The Receiver dispatches the notification
  to the right local Coordination Task
  (one extra lookup under the broad
  Subscription strategy).
  notification-authorization-hint scopes
  the pull to this patient + dataset.
end note

== CW: Fulfiller starts work (write-back) ==
F -> P ++: PUT Coordination Task\n(Task.businessStatus = in-progress)
P --> F --: 200 OK

== Loop: BgZ updates during the workflow ==
loop While the Coordination Task is in-progress
  P -> P : BgZ data at the Placer changes;\nPlacer updates the List\n(entry added / removed / version bumped)
  P -> F ++: POST notification Bundle\nfocus = List (event-number incremented)\nadditional-context = changed entries (optional)
  F --> P --: 200 OK
  F -> P ++: GET refreshed entries\n(or _lastUpdated-filtered against the List)
  P --> F --: 200 OK
end

== CW: Fulfiller completes (write-back) ==
F -> P ++: PUT Coordination Task\n(Task.status = completed,\nTask.businessStatus = completed,\nTask.output = outcome document)
P --> F --: 200 OK
note over P #FFF2CC: List for this offer may be retained for audit (later pulls return 410 when actually withdrawn)\nor deleted. Both Subscriptions remain active for the partnership.

@enduml
